cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  nf-claw was created by Danilo Monge. The pipelines it serves are authored by
  the nf-core community — the core of the library — and are wrapped unmodified;
  nf-claw also adapts some files and its repository structure from ClawBio
  (created by Manuel Corpas). If you use nf-claw, please cite it using the
  metadata below, together with Nextflow, the nf-core framework, and especially
  the specific nf-core pipeline you ran (see references).
type: software
title: "nf-claw: A self-maintaining, token-minimal library of nf-core pipelines for AI agents"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-06-15"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  nf-claw turns nf-core pipelines into an agent-runnable library. The pipelines
  themselves are authored by the nf-core community and wrapped unmodified as
  git submodules pinned to a release tag; nf-claw pairs each with an
  auto-generated, token-minimal skill.md (the exact run command and required
  inputs) and a full reference.md, derived from pinned schemas, usage documents
  and citations. A generic runner executes each pipeline through a single command
  and records a provenance bundle; curated, schema-checked handoff rules chain
  pipelines. Documented runtime corrections preserve the pinned source trees
  and record their evidence for replay. Scheduled workflows track release tags
  through git and merge updates only after acceptance, test and drift checks pass.
keywords:
  - nextflow
  - nf-core
  - bioinformatics
  - pipelines
  - workflows
  - AI agents
  - reproducibility
  - automation
authors:
  - family-names: Monge
    given-names: Danilo
    affiliation: "Eberhard Karls Universität Tübingen"
